issues.body:
#### Technical Details

[`BridgeDepositStrategy.depositFromSickle()`](https://github.com/vfat-io/sickle-contracts/blob/44aa74fefac5d760a0d6f0003f103689f13ddeae/contracts/strategies/BridgeDepositStrategy.sol#L238) is intended to cap consumption of the declared bridge token by measuring `balanceBefore - balanceAfter` on that token and reverting with `ManualDepositAmountExceeded` if the consumed amount exceeds the caller-supplied `amount`.

However, the function does not isolate user-supplied funds from third-party dust already present in the victim Sickle. If an attacker transfers even `1 wei` of the same `token` to the victim Sickle before the manual deposit executes, that dust is included in `balanceBefore`.

This becomes exploitable when the same `token` is also present in `params.sweepTokens`, because [`TransferLib.transferTokensToUser()`](https://github.com/vfat-io/sickle-contracts/blob/44aa74fefac5d760a0d6f0003f103689f13ddeae/contracts/libraries/TransferLib.sol#L56) transfers the full token balance of the Sickle to the owner. In that case the dusted `1 wei` is also consumed by the flow, so the post-check observes `consumed = amount + 1` and the transaction reverts even though the caller only intended to spend `amount`.

#### Impact

Low. An attacker can cheaply grief `depositFromSickle()` by dusting the victim Sickle with a negligible amount of the input token, causing otherwise valid manual bridge deposits to revert when that same token is swept. This is a DoD vector against the manual destination-side recovery path.

**PoC**

```solidity
function test_depositFromSickle_reverts_when_consumption_exceeds_amount_dos() public {
    uint256 balance = 1000e18;
    token.mint(address(ctx.sickle), balance);

    address attacker = makeAddr("attacker");
    token.mint(address(attacker), balance);
    vm.prank(attacker);
    token.transfer(address(ctx.sickle), 1);

    BridgeDepositStrategy.DepositParams memory params =
        _emptyDepositParams();
    params.sweepTokens = new address[](1);
    params.sweepTokens[0] = address(token);

    vm.prank(sickleOwner);
    vm.expectRevert(
        BridgeDepositStrategy.ManualDepositAmountExceeded.selector
    );
    strategy.depositFromSickle(address(token), 1000e18, params);

    assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(ctx.sickle)), balance + 1);
    assertEq(token.balanceOf(sickleOwner), 0);
}
```

#### Recommendation

Do not allow token sweeping in `depositFromSickle()`. Alternatively, since sweeping residual token balances is not a core functionality, clearly document this behavior so users can choose whether to include sweeping in the manual deposit flow.

#### Developer Response

Fixed in [PR#680](https://github.com/vfat-io/sickle-contracts/pull/680) (merge commit [298bdca2](https://github.com/vfat-io/sickle-contracts/commit/298bdca2e4e3fa13ee333a1ef75153c8ff076e5a)). The accepted final form is in commit [505d69fb](https://github.com/vfat-io/sickle-contracts/commit/505d69fbd8405fdd7a897a7119fe18355bca9666) — refactor: simplify `depositFromSickle` to just execute deposit and sweep leftovers — which removes the balance-before/after accounting (and the `ManualDepositAmountExceeded` error) entirely, so dust donations no longer cause a revert.
